---
/**
 * Plain-language description of what the product is and what it does with a
 * user's Gmail account, written for a Google OAuth verification reviewer
 * checking that the app's purpose and name are stated on a public page.
 * Deliberately prose-only, no marketing sections - the shell, typography, and
 * theme tokens are the same ones /privacy and /terms use.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config/landing";
---

<Base
  title={`About ${site.name}`}
  description={`What ${site.name} is, what it does with your Gmail account, and which permissions it asks for.`}
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 leading-relaxed sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm opacity-70 hover:opacity-100">&larr; Back to {site.name}</a>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold">{site.name}</h1>

    <p class="mt-8">
      {site.name} connects your Gmail account to the AI client you already use.
      Ask what needs your attention and get a ranked inbox. Archive threads and
      mark them done. Draft a reply in a real composer, edit it yourself, and
      send it &mdash; inside Claude, ChatGPT, or any MCP client.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6">
      To do this, {site.name} asks permission to read, organise, draft, and send
      mail in your Gmail account. It never permanently deletes mail and never
      bypasses Trash. Message content is fetched only when you ask for it and is
      passed to your AI client; we do not store message bodies, and no AI model
      on our servers reads your mail. You can disconnect at any time, which
      revokes the token with Google and erases it from our database.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6">
      Read our
      <a class="underline decoration-from-font underline-offset-2" href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>
      and
      <a class="underline decoration-from-font underline-offset-2" href="/terms">terms of service</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
